        }
      ],
      "content": "a kind of light armour, first used in Germany, in which great flexibility was obtained by overlapping plates sliding on rivets (OED s.v. almain-rivets); the Cologne translation adds that this armour was for the use of foot-soldiers (Deutsche knecht harnish)"
    }
